    "q-340668": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340668",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
